  ```python
  class SlowAPIMiddleware:
      async def __call__(self, scope, receive, send):
          ...
          app = scope["app"]
          limiter = app.state.limiter
          handler = None
          # get route name
          ...
          name = endpoint.__name__ if endpoint else None
          # check if exempt
          if limiter._is_exempt(...): return
          # check limits
          try:
              limiter._check_request_limit(request, endpoint, in_middleware=True)
          except RateLimitExceeded ...
  ```

  And `_check_request_limit`: it gathers limits for the route: explicit limits from decorated route; if none and `in_middleware`, it applies `self._default_limits` when... Looking at slowapi Limiter._check_request_limit: 

